   "rule_summary": "Manufacturers must report every thermal incident involving fire, smoke, uncontrolled overheating, or emergency intervention to the relevant regulator within 24 hours of learning of it, with a fuller incident report within 10 business days. Affected customers must be notified within 72 hours when an incident presents a credible safety risk to their unit or requires inspection, service, or precautions.",
   "comparison": "all parameters safe or better",
   "final_rule_text": "Manufacturers must report every thermal incident involving fire, smoke, uncontrolled overheating, or emergency intervention to the relevant regulator within 24 hours of learning of it, with a fuller incident report within 10 business days. Affected customers must be notified within 72 hours when an incident presents a credible safety risk to their unit or requires inspection, service, or precautions. Reports must include known facts and be updated as investigations progress; uncertainty does not delay initial reporting."
