   "rule_summary": "A model passes if no more than 10% of tested units fail. Customers who buy a model receive its pass/fail status, but not its per-model failure rate.",
   "comparison": "weakened by: permanent_limit_pct, over_limit_consequence",
   "final_rule_text": "Each model must undergo a sustained-heat test at 55 °C using a regulator-approved protocol before market entry, at least every three years, and after a material design change. A model passes if no more than 10% of tested units fail. Manufacturers must provide test methods, sample sizes, and full per-model results, including failure rates, to the relevant regulator. Customers who buy a model receive its pass/fail status, but not its per-model failure rate. Regulators may require corrective action or retesting where results indicate a safety concern."
  },
